# Project: Self-Study Course "pyenv + venv + Jupyter Notebook"

## Overview

A self-paced course on managing the Python environment in Linux (Ubuntu-based).
Tools: **pyenv**, **venv**, **pip**, **Jupyter Notebook**, **JupyterLab**.
Published on GitHub as markdown files. All course content is in Russian.

## Target Audience

- Knows Python, advanced terminal skills.
- No prior experience with pyenv, venv, or similar tools.
- OS: **Linux Ubuntu-based only** (Kubuntu).

## Module Sequence (12 modules)

| # | Module | Dir |
|---|--------|-----|
| 0 | Python environment in Linux | `00-python-environment/` |
| 1 | pyenv: installation & basics | `01-pyenv-basics/` |
| 2 | pyenv: version management | `02-pyenv-advanced/` |
| 3 | pip & package management | `03-pip/` |
| 4 | venv: creation & usage | `04-venv-basics/` |
| 5 | venv: advanced usage | `05-venv-advanced/` |
| 6 | Jupyter Notebook | `06-jupyter-notebook/` |
| 7 | Jupyter: kernels & integration | `07-jupyter-kernels/` |
| 8 | Jupyter: hands-on practice | `08-jupyter-practice/` |
| 9 | JupyterLab | `09-jupyterlab/` |
| 10 | Project practice | `10-project-practice/` |
| 11 | Integration: end-to-end scenarios | `11-integration/` |

## File Structure

- Course root: `course/`
- Module dir: `course/NN-name/`
- Unit dir: `course/NN-module/NN-unit-name/`
- Unit main file: `README.md`
- Reference solutions: `solution.md`
- Check scripts: `check.sh`
- Break scripts (diagnostic labs): `break.sh`
- Pre-made notebooks (practice module): `*.ipynb`
- Media: in unit dir next to README.md
- Cheatsheets: `course/cheatsheets/`
- Glossary: `course/references/glossary.md`
- Terminal commands: `course/references/terminal-commands.md`

## Unit Type Naming Convention

Unit directory names encode the type:
- **Lessons**: no prefix — `01-system-python/`, `03-basic-usage/`
- **Labs**: `*-lab-*/` — `05-lab-install-and-switch/`
- **Diagnostic labs**: `*-lab-debug-*/` — `13-lab-debug-missing-python/`
- **Trainers**: `*-trainer-*/` — `02-trainer-installation/`
- **Tests**: `*-test-*/` — `05-test-versions/`

## Terminology Policy

The course uses professional terminology without fear:
1. **First mention** — term is defined inline + added to `course/references/glossary.md`.
2. **Subsequent uses** — term is used freely, with a footnote linking to the glossary.
3. Never re-explain a previously defined term in the main text.

## Practice Placement (Snowball Principle)

Tests and labs grouped after every 2–3 lessons. Each practice unit covers:
- Newly learned topics.
- Previously learned topics from the same module.
One practice unit per lesson is NOT the pattern.

## Verification System

Self-check (expected output) + `check.sh` (bash) + `solution.md` (mandatory for every lab).

## Navigation

- `course/README.md` — table of contents.
- Every unit `README.md` has `← Назад` and `Далее →` links.

## Roles

- **Methodologist** (AI): structure, completeness, sequencing, practice coverage, review.
- **Author / Client** (Aleksey): goals, approval, acceptance.

## AI Agent Constraints

- **DO NOT interact with git.**
- New terminal commands → short reference (1–2 sentences) + add to `course/references/terminal-commands.md`.
- New terms → define inline + add to `course/references/glossary.md`.
- Each file is a self-contained learning unit.
- **Always respond in Russian.**
